# AddressSanitizer / UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for YARS.
#
# Format: `<sanitizer>:<symbol-substring>` — see clang docs at
# https://clang.llvm.org/docs/AddressSanitizer.html#suppressing-reports-in-external-libraries
#
# Activate via:
#   export ASAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=$(pwd)/suppressions/asan.supp"
#
# Current state (2026-05-12): empty — the audit run on
# branch `feat/linux-ci-verification` found no third-party (Ogre/Bullet/Xerces)
# false positives that warranted a suppression. The four YARS-attributable
# findings are tracked as follow-up fix proposals; see
# docs/planning/memory-safety-audit-status.md.
#
# When adding a suppression, include:
#   * date added
#   * the sanitizer event (file:line + summary)
#   * why it is a false positive or third-party issue
#   * the upstream tracking link (if any)
